course: dictionary
lesson: 4777
title: Huddle: close together, close to warm
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: To huddle means to crowd close together, usually to keep warm, feel safe or talk secretly. Read the clues around the word. «Male emperor penguins huddle in thousands» tells you they are packed close together in the cold.
explain: The sentence «the children huddled round the fire» gives another clue. Children on a cold night, or scared, or sharing a secret, would sit close together. So huddled shows cold, fear or secrecy. Try your meaning in the sentence: "the children crowded close round the fire" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Huddle can also be a noun, meaning a small, close group. In sports, a team huddle is when players gather close to plan the next play. The word changes its form, but the idea of being close together stays the same.
fact: To huddle means to crowd close together, usually to keep warm, to feel safe or to talk secretly.
fact: To huddle can also mean to curl your body up small, as in «huddled under a blanket».
fact: A huddle is a small, close group of people or animals.
fact: In sports, a team huddle is when players gather close to plan the next move.
fact: Inside an emperor penguin huddle it can be more than 20 degrees warmer than outside, so huddling really helps them stay warm.
exercise: «Male emperor penguins huddle in thousands, each with an egg on his feet.» What does huddle mean here? | *Crowd close together | Sing loudly | Walk away alone | Fly very high
exercise: «The children huddled round the fire.» What does huddled suggest? | Bored of the game | Hot and sweaty | Very tall | *Cold, fear or secrecy
exercise: In American football, the players go into a ... to plan the next play. Which word fits? | blanket | *huddle | whisper | castle
test: «Golden snub-nosed monkeys huddle together in the snow.» What does huddle mean? | Stretch out far apart | *Crowd close together | Swim under water | Run away fast
test: In a sentence, what is a huddle as a noun? | A tall, thin tree | A long road | *A small, close group of people or animals | A loud shout
exam: Why do emperor penguins huddle through the Antarctic winter? | To hunt fish in the sea | *To keep warm in the freezing cold | To build nests in trees | To race across the ice
